{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794991355,"nonce":"lcmR72bdrDFeb5jYqqDTTD2GGww=","title":"Remote URI assets and typed HTTP/WS/WSS streams","message":"Support explicitly dynamic @:asset declarations over HTTP(S) URIs and typed AssetStream\u003cT\u003e fields over WS(S), plus HTTP byte-chunk streams. Keep compilation offline; decoded embedded assets remain the default for known local data. Use mature verified-TLS native clients and the existing page-owned browser mailbox, returning results through hxn.Future. A stream has one pending reader, bounded frame/queue sizes, explicit close/cancellation, preserved message boundaries and no unbounded cache or automatic reconnect. HTTP transport chunks are not application records; require byte streams or an explicit framing decoder. Generate ownership/cleanup when an asset group unloads, reloads, fails or is superseded. RemoteSource can borrow a local fallback source; authentication/options are application supplied. Native private-CA trust is explicit; browser trust is controlled by the browser. Validate HTTP(S), WS/WSS, empty/fragmented messages, EOF/error ordering, size/backpressure limits, cancellation and TLS verification with local fixtures on native and all three browser configurations. Keep CRDT state/merge/sync protocols separate, tracked in 5b44833.","files":null}]}